From: our reconstruction (upstream MPTCP, Linux 5.6+)
Subject: [PATCH] tcp: move the MPTCP skb extension when collapsing

GL.iNet's 4.6.x/4.7.x kernels call mptcp_skb_ext_move() in tcp_collapse(),
as upstream MPTCP does; their later published compat patch (4.8.6) doesn't.
Only with this call does tcp_collapse have GL.iNet's size (single-object
compile, validated against our vmlinux).

---
--- a/net/ipv4/tcp_input.c
+++ b/net/ipv4/tcp_input.c
@@ -5031,6 +5031,7 @@
 		else
 			__skb_queue_tail(&tmp, nskb); /* defer rbtree insertion */
 		skb_set_owner_r(nskb, sk);
+		mptcp_skb_ext_move(nskb, skb);
 
 		/* Copy data, releasing collapsed skbs. */
 		while (copy > 0) {
